CURRENT DATA ORGANIZATIONS AND ACCESS FUNCTIONS IN C AND C++
------------------------------------------------------------

This file lists all available classes (data organizations)
and the methods (functions) to operate on the data.
The C functions (left column) are implemented through CPP macros
and code generated functions.
The C++ functions (right column) are implemented through pure
C++ classes. There is no hierarchy of classes; classes are not derived
from a common base class, they are 'flat'. Each class is represented
by an interface class that contains no data, only the methods.

If some data organizations which you need are missing, you can
easily add it to the library. Everything is in source.

